treePref               package:AA                    R Documentation

Data on Cattle Grazing

Description:

     The 'treePref' data frame has 256 rows and 5 columns.

     In this experiment, sixteen square plots of side 8 metres were
     chosen randomly in each of two fields, and eight tree seedlings
     were planted at the mid-points and corners of each plot. The
     seedlings comprised four species of tree, fir, maple, beech, and
     spruce, in pairs, one 20 cm and one 60 cm in height.  Herds of
     cows were introduced into the two fields, and after a period it
     was observed whether or not each seedling had been grazed.  

     This is a split-plot experiment in which the sub-plot design is a
     4 x 2 factorial (species x height) and the response is binary
     (grazed or ungrazed), but with the two fields and hence the plots
     within them subject to different grazing pressures, owing to the
     different sizes.  There are in alla 256 responses in this
     experiment.

Usage:

     data(treePref)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'Field' a factor variable for the field (13/23);

     'Blockk' a factor variable for the block (1-32);

     'Species' a factor variable for the seedling species (Abies, Acer,
          Fagus, Picea);

     'Height' a factor variable for the seedling height (Small/Large);

     'State' the response variable of this experiment
          (Grazed/Ungrazed).

Source:

     The data were obtained from two experiments conducted in the
     summer of 2003 by Charlotte Vandenberghe, Francois Frelechoux and
     colleagues of the Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and
     Landscape Research.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 6.3.
